  "title": "Nasdaq Report Identifies Between $25 Billion and $50 Billion in Potential Efficiency Gains in Banks' Risk and Compliance Functions",
  "summary": "--Between $25 billion and $50 billion in potential efficiency gains can be realized through targeted enhancements in banks' Risk and Compliance functions alone without compromising effectiveness, according to a report released by Nasdaq and Boston Consulting Group. What’ s more, regulators have put banks on the front line in the fight against financial crime...",
